AHS-004 — Overall Architecture

Document ID: AHS-004
Title: Overall Architecture
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

Architectural Views: Conceptual, Logical

1. Purpose

This specification defines the canonical high-level architecture of the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

It establishes the major architectural layers, core components, and interaction model that collectively implement engineering cognition as defined by the Atlas Core Concepts (ACC).

The Overall Architecture provides the primary structural blueprint for all Atlas implementations.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Architectural layers
Core architectural components
System boundaries
High-level interactions
Architectural responsibilities
External interfaces

This specification does not define internal algorithms or implementation technologies.

3. Architectural Objectives

The Atlas architecture SHALL:

Implement all canonical concepts defined by ACC.
Preserve conceptual integrity.
Support modular implementation.
Enable explainable engineering cognition.
Scale from a single engineering workstation to distributed enterprise deployments.
Remain independent of implementation technologies.
4. Architectural Philosophy

Atlas is designed as a layered cognitive architecture.

Each layer performs a distinct responsibility while exposing well-defined services to adjacent layers.

No layer SHALL bypass another unless explicitly permitted by this specification.

This layered approach promotes:

Separation of concerns
Replaceable implementations
Predictable information flow
Easier testing and validation
Long-term maintainability
